Spec: Project/Flows

Purpose:
  Define how THIS project normally moves work between engineering
  stages — the concrete, project-level instance of the chain engine.
  This is NOT the chain engine itself (bax chains/chains.sdd, ENGINE
  layer) and NOT a domain's real flow (bax project/<domain>/flows.sdd,
  not yet created — forward reference, no domain exists yet).

  Three layers, not to be confused:

    chains/chains.sdd            -> "HOW DOES THE CHAIN WORK?" (generic engine)
    project/flows.sdd            -> "WHAT IS THIS PROJECT'S DEFAULT FLOW?" (this file)
    project/<domain>/flows.sdd   -> "WHAT IS THE REAL FLOW FOR <DOMAIN>?" (concrete, future)


Owns:
  This project's default stage sequence
  Project-level flow rules


DoesNotOwn:
  Chain lifecycle rules and stage definitions   (see ../chains/chains.sdd)
  Domain-specific flow overrides                (see project/<domain>/flows.sdd, future)
  Feature-level chain type selection            (see ./project.sdd -> [PM4])


Stages:

  AN, AR, DB, BE, API, FE, MD, QA, DO, VR

  (reusing chains/chains.sdd's own Stages vocabulary — discipline stages
  DB/BE/API/FE/MD/QA/DO, orchestration stages AN/AR, final verification
  VR — not redefined here, bax chains/chains.sdd -> Stages.)


Default:

  AN > AR > DB > BE > API > FE > MD > QA > DO > VR


Rules:

  [F1]
  This file defines this project's default flow, not the chain engine
  itself.

  [F2]
  Global chain lifecycle rules remain owned by chains/chains.sdd — this
  file MUST NOT redefine them.

  [F3]
  A domain flow (project/<domain>/flows.sdd) MAY override the default
  sequence above when justified by that domain's own dependencies.

  [F4]
  A feature flow MAY add or remove stages from the default sequence
  based on its own dependency analysis.

  [F5]
  VR MUST remain the final verification stage in any resolved flow,
  regardless of domain/feature overrides.

  [F6]
  Flow changes (default sequence, domain overrides, feature overrides)
  MUST be traceable — recorded via decisions/decisions.sdd or state/
  state.sdd, not silently changed.


FlowResolution:

  Global chain rules (chains/chains.sdd)
    > Project flow (this file)
    > Domain flow (project/<domain>/flows.sdd)
    > Feature-specific stage overrides
    > Final executable chain

  (mirrors the ENGINE > MODEL resolution pattern already used by
  chains/chains.sdd -> FlowResolution and architecture/principles.sdd
  -> Resolution — root stays reusable, the project model carries the
  concrete instance.)


Portability:

  This file's Default sequence is this project's own instance and is
  NOT expected to be reusable as-is across other projects — unlike
  chains/chains.sdd, which MUST remain project-agnostic.


Navigation:
  Chain engine:     @../chains/chains.sdd
  Project model:     @./project.sdd
  Domain flow:        @./<domain>/flows.sdd (future, no domain exists yet)


State: STEP 14

Note:
  (prompt/new/36.md — source labeled this "STEP 13", the same
  third-consecutive mislabel collision noted in ./project.sdd -> Note;
  this repo's own sequential count treats it as STEP 14, bax
  ../PROJECT.sdd -> Note.)

  This file resolves a double dangling forward-reference that existed
  since STEP 11/12: chains/chains.sdd -> ProjectFlow already pointed at
  `@../project/flows.sdd`, and project/map.sdd -> Navigation already
  routed through a flow step, but no such file existed yet (bax
  chains/chains.sdd -> ProjectFlow's own prior note, now stale and
  corrected as part of this same STEP — bax ../chains/chains.sdd ->
  Note). This file is the first genuinely new file this STEP creates
  with no existing-file collision (contrast ./project.sdd, which
  collided with domains.sdd/modules.sdd's territory, and map.sdd/
  dependencies.sdd/indexes.sdd, left untouched — bax ./project.sdd ->
