  Rule IDs: the source's bare `[F1]-[F6]` range was confirmed free
  against every other prefix in this repo ([R] PROJECT, [C] chains,
  [T] tasks, [D] decisions, [S] state, [AP] architecture principles,
  [P] prompts, [PM] project model) — kept as-is, no renumbering needed.

  Deliberate departures from the source spec, per the standing "apply,
  don't copy" rule: added an explicit Owns/DoesNotOwn pair (absent from
  the source) stating this file does NOT redefine chain lifecycle rules
   or domain-level overrides, matching this repo's established per-file
  convention (see architecture/principles.sdd -> DoesNotOwn); added a
  FlowResolution section mirroring chains.sdd's own FlowResolution and
  principles.sdd -> Resolution, since the source described this
  three-layer relationship only in prose (see "Most important point" in
  the source chunk) without a matching structured Resolution block; folded
  the source's separate "AN/AR/.../VR" Stages list into a one-line
  reference to chains.sdd's own Stages vocabulary rather than
  redeclaring it a second time (see NoDuplication, architecture/
  architecture.sdd -> Principles).

BusinessFlows:

  IntegrationExecution:
    purpose: End-to-end flow for executing an external integration call
    applies_to:
      - sweeps-integrations
      - pultapaz
    steps:
      - receive_event: Event/message arrives (WebSocket, RabbitMQ, HTTP webhook, or polling claim)
      - validate_payload: Validate required fields (target_service, event_type, action_json)
      - check_conditions: Evaluate integration conditions (amount, duration, employment status)
      - execute_precheck: Validate identity against external API (optional, config-driven)
      - build_request: Map internal fields to external API format using field mapping + transforms
      - call_external_api: Execute HTTP request with auth, timeout, content-type handling
      - process_response: Map external response back to internal fields
      - log_result: Persist request/response/execution_time to integration_log
      - notify_if_needed: Dispatch notification if integration triggers one (email, slack, sms)
    error_handling:
      - retry_on_failure: Increment retry_count, schedule retry with backoff
      - dead_letter: After max retries, mark as failed and alert
      - partial_success: Batch operations may partially succeed
    variants:
      - proactive_forward: pultapaz sends quiz data to bank without prior request
      - reactive_webhook: External system calls back with result
      - status_poll: Periodic check of application status

  NotificationDispatch:
    purpose: Send outbound notifications through configured channels
    applies_to:
      - sweeps-integrations
      - pultapaz
    steps:
      - resolve_template: Load template config from settings (html_template, fields_to_replace)
      - render_content: Replace placeholders with actual data values
      - check_daily_limit: Verify integration has not exceeded daily send limit
      - send_via_provider: Execute send through configured provider (Mailgun, SMTP, Slack webhook, SMS, Telegram)
      - log_result: Record send status, provider response, execution time
    error_handling:
      - retry_on_failure: Queue for retry (async via RabbitMQ or direct retry)
      - daily_limit_skip: Log and skip, do not retry
      - provider_fallback: Try alternative provider if primary fails
    variants:
      - async_mail: Queued via RabbitMQ for background processing
      - sync_notify: Immediate send (Slack webhook, Telegram)
      - template_email: HTML template with dynamic field replacement

  ScheduledSync:
    purpose: Periodic synchronization of external configuration data
    applies_to:
      - sweeps-integrations
    steps:
      - fetch_config_once: Single API call to retrieve full app configuration
      - execute_handlers_sequentially: Run sync handlers one by one to avoid DB contention
      - log_results: Record sync statistics (counts, errors, duration)
    handlers:
      - sync_levels: User level definitions
      - sync_avatars: Player avatar assets
      - sync_tournaments: Tournament configurations
      - sync_missions: Mission/badge definitions
    variants:
      - full_sync: All handlers run on every cycle
      - incremental_sync: Only changed items updated (future)

  WebSocketEventIngestion:
    purpose: Real-time event intake via WebSocket with database persistence
    applies_to:
      - sweeps-integrations
    steps:
      - connect: Establish WebSocket connection with auth (app_id + secret)
      - heartbeat: Send periodic ping, expect pong response
      - receive_message: Parse incoming JSON message (auid + events array)
      - deduplicate: Check auid against acknowledged set to prevent duplicates
      - persist_to_db: Store raw event in websocket_events table via RPC
      - acknowledge: Send auid back to provider to confirm receipt
      - auto_restart: Periodic reconnect every 24h to prevent stale connections
    error_handling:
      - reconnect_on_close: Exponential backoff up to max attempts
      - fallback_to_polling: If WebSocket fails, activate polling loop
      - db_triggers: Database triggers auto-process persisted events

  BatchPreCheck:
    purpose: Validate customer identity against multiple integrations in parallel
    applies_to:
      - pultapaz
    steps:
      - receive_job: BatchPreCheckResult job created with identity values (phone, fin, seria)
      - discover_integrations: Find all active integrations with pre_check configured
      - execute_checks: Run pre-check for each integration sequentially or in parallel
      - aggregate_results: Collect pass/fail counts per integration
      - update_job_status: Mark BatchPreCheckResult as completed with statistics
    error_handling:
      - integration_failure: Individual integration failure does not block others
      - timeout_per_integration: Each pre-check has its own timeout (10-30s)
      - partial_results: Store whatever results were collected

State: +

